          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em integer Heisenberg groups
            or
            %em discrete Heisenberg groups
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+group"} non-abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extensions"} central extensions
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+groups"} product groups
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}^{2g}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in \mathbb{N}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+groups"} Heisenberg groups
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+group"} non-abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extensions"} central extensions
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{2g}
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              \-Heisenberg groups
            for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            In fact, for even multiples of the basic such extension, integer Heisenberg groups are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            of ordinary
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+groups"} Heisenberg groups
            covering a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+%28discrete+subgroup%29"} lattice
            inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi g
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}^{2g} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{2g}
            (cf. Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TwiceHeisenbergExtensionInSymplecticForm"}
            below).
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+D%3D3+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+Chern-Simons+theory"} abelian Chern-Simons theory
            (spelled out
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ModularAutomorphisms"} below
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#SS25"} SS25
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "cohomotopy#CohomotopyModuliOfSurfaces"} 2-Cohomotopy moduli of surfaces
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %h3#IntegerHeisenbergGroup
            Integer Heisenberg group extensions of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}^2
          %p
            We discuss the restriction of the basic
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+group"} Heisenberg group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Heisenberg+group#H3InComponents"} there
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}^2 \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^2
            and the mod-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+groups"} quotient groups
            of that.
          %p
            In the following, we denote
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+groups"} cyclic groups
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "left center left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℤ
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtd
                          %mi k
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mtd
                          %mtext otherwise
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{Z}_{k}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\left\{
                  \\begin{array}{lcl}
                  \\mathbb{Z} &amp;\vert&amp; k = 0
                  \\\
                  \\mathbb{Z}/(k) &amp;\vert&amp; \text{otherwise}
                  \\mathrlap{\,.}
                  \\end{array}
                  \\right.
          %p
            Recall (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "group+extension#CentralExtensionClassificationByGroupCohomology"} there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extensions"} central extensions
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            (for the present case equipped with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+action"} trivial
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ;
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^2(G;A)
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extension"} central
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extensions"} group extensions
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}^2
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_k
              are all integral multiples of the following elementary Heisenberg extension:
            #eq:BasicIntegerHeisenbergExtensionOfZ2.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mi b
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ∈
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo ×
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mi k
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ,
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mi b
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo ′
                            %mo ,
                            %mi b
                            %mo ′
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo =
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo +
                            %mi a
                            %mo ′
                            %mo ,
                            %mi b
                            %mo +
                            %mi b
                            %mo ′
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mi n
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mstyle{:mathcolor => "red"}
                              %mi a
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi b
                              %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    \\begin{array}{l}
                    \\big(a,b,[n]\big)
                    \\,\in\,
                    \\mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{Z}_{k}
                    \\,,
                    \\\
                    \\big(
                    a,b,[n]
                    \\big)
                    \\cdot
                    \\big(
                    a',b',[n']
                    \\big)
                    \\;=\;
                    \\big(
                    a + a',
                    b + b',
                    [
                    n + n' +
                    {\color{red}
                    a \, b'
                    }
                    ]
                    \\big)
                    \\end{array}
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extensions"} central extensions
              in question
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi k
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi cntrl
                    %mi H
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    1
                    \\to
                    \\mathbb{Z}_k
                    \\xrightarrow{cntrl}
                    H
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbb{Z}^2
                    \\to
                    1
            %p
              %a{:href => "group+extension#CentralExtensionClassificationByGroupCohomology"} are classified
              by the degree=2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}^2
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_k
              (equipped with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+action"} trivial
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}^2
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} action
            %p
              That second
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
              is:
            #eq:SecondGroupCohomologyOfZPlusZ.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi H
                            %mi Grp
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ;
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi B
                          %msup
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ;
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi T
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ;
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msubsup
                            %mi S
                            %mi a
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ∨
                          %msubsup
                            %mi S
                            %mi b
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ∨
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ;
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ;
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mi k
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{ccl}
                    H^2_{Grp}(\mathbb{Z}^2;\, \mathbb{Z}_k)
                    \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                    H^2(B \mathbb{Z}^2;\, \mathbb{Z}_k)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                    H^2(T^2;\, \mathbb{Z}_k)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                    H^2(S^1_a \vee S^1_b \vee S^2;\, \mathbb{Z}_k)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                    H^2(S^2;\, \mathbb{Z}_k)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                    \\mathbb{Z}_k
                    \\mathrlap{\,,}
                    \\end{array}
            %p where we used, in order of the appearance:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  that
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
                  of the domain group’s
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
              %li
                %p
                  that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
                  and that this respects
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
              %li
                %p
                  that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+type"} stable homotopy type
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-torus"} 2-torus
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
                  of two
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circles"} circles
                  with a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
                  (see
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a{:href => "torus#AsAHomotopyType"} there
            %p
              The generator of this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+group"} cohomology group
              must be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group 2-cocycle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi Grp
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ;
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\alpha \,\in\, H^2_{Grp}\big(
                    \\mathbb{Z}^2
                    ;\,
                    \\mathbb{Z}_k
                    \\big)
            %p given by
            #eq:IntegerHeisenbergExtension.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ×
                          %msup
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi α
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mi n
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ′
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi a
                          %mi b
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{ccc}
                    \\mathbb{Z}^2
                    \\times
                    \\mathbb{Z}^2
                    \&amp;\xrightarrow{\; \alpha \;}&amp;
                    \\mathbb{Z}_{n}
                    \\\
                    \\big(
                    (a,b), (a',b')
                    \\big)
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    [ a b']
                    \\mathrlap{\,,}
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              whose cocycle condition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi a
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo +
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi b
                    %mo ″
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mi b
                    %mo ″
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mi b
                    %mo ″
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [a b'] + [(a+a')b'']
                    \=
                    [a(b'+b'')] + [a' b'']
              is evidently satisfied due to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+law"} distributive law
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              and which is clearly not divisible.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              In the integer Heisenberg group
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BasicIntegerHeisenbergExtensionOfZ2"} (1)
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+elements"} inverse elements
                  are given by
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %msup
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo −
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\big(a ,\, b ,\, [n]\big)^{-1}
                        \\;=\;
                        \\big(
                        \-a ,\, -b ,\, [-n + a b]
                        \\big)
              %li
                %p
                  the basic
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+commutators"} group commutators
                  give
                #eq:BasicGroupCommutator.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
